"Let $d_k(n)$ be the minimum number of arcs in a $k$-dicritical digraph of order $n$, and let $o_k(n)$ be the minimum number of arcs in a $k$-dicritical oriented graph of order $n$, with value $+\\infty$ when no such oriented graph exists. **Kostochka–Stiebitz gap conjecture.** There exists $\\varepsilon>0$ such that\n\n$$\no_k(n)\\geq(1+\\varepsilon)\\cdot d_k(n)\n$$\n\nfor every $k\\geq4$ and sufficiently large $n$. The conjecture asserts a uniform asymptotic density gap between arbitrary and oriented $k$-dicritical digraphs; the source notes that it is known for $k=3$ and $k=4$, but remains open for general $k$."